#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:0
msgid ""
"Use the snapd REST API to integrate TPM-FDE into a custom Ubuntu installer, "
"including pre-install checks and fixes, PIN or passphrase setup, and "
"preseeding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:8
msgid "Integrate TPM-FDE into a custom Ubuntu installer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:10
msgid ""
"This guide shows you how to integrate [hardware-backed Full Disk Encryption]"
"(https://ubuntu.com/desktop/docs/en/latest/explanation/hardware-backed-disk-"
"encryption/#hardware-backed-disk-encryption) (TPM-FDE) into a custom Ubuntu "
"installer using the snapd REST API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:12
msgid ""
"Refer to the {ref}`snapd REST API reference<reference-development-snapd-rest-"
"api>` for a list of all API actions and endpoints. For general instructions, "
"refer to the {ref}`guide on how to use the REST API<how-to-guides-manage-"
"snaps-use-the-rest-api>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:14
msgid "Follow the steps in order. Some steps are optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:16
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:18
msgid ""
"To follow this guide, your installer must have access to a recovery system "
"seed available to snapd. A recovery system seed is the set of files that "
"describes the Ubuntu system to be installed. It includes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:19
msgid ""
"a [model assertion](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/core/reference/"
"assertions/model/) describing the Ubuntu system to install; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:20
msgid ""
"the essential snaps making up that system, including the [base](https://"
"documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/reference/bases/), {ref}"
"`kernel<reference-development-yaml-schemas-the-kernel-snap>`, {ref}"
"`gadget<reference-development-yaml-schemas-the-gadget-snap>`, and {ref}"
"`snapd<ref-glossary_snapd>` snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:22
msgid ""
"To get Canonical's reference model for the Ubuntu release used in this "
"guide, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:23
msgid ""
"snap known model --remote series=16 brand-id=canonical model=ubuntu-"
"classic-2604-amd64\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:27
msgid "For more information, see:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:28
msgid ""
"[Create a model](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/core/tutorials/build-your-"
"first-image/create-a-model/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:29
msgid ""
"[Create a recovery system from the API](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/"
"core/how-to-guides/manage-ubuntu-core/create-a-recovery-system-from-the-api/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:31
msgid ""
"To learn about the layout of a recovery system seed, see also [Ubuntu Core "
"storage layout](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/core/explanation/core-"
"elements/storage-layout/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:33
msgid "Get system label"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:35
msgid ""
"Each recovery system is identified by a unique label, corresponding to its "
"directory in the installer seed. Normally, this directory is `/var/lib/snapd/"
"seed/systems/<label>/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:37
msgid ""
"To get the system label, make a `GET` request to `/v2/systems`. Snapd will "
"return a synchronous response (`200 OK`) with a list of all the available "
"systems, including their labels. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:40
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:73
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:96
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:157
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:176
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:424
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:442
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:515
msgid "Response body, `result`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:40
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  ...\n"
"  \"systems\": [\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"current\": true,\n"
"      \"default-recovery-system\": true,\n"
"      \"label\": \"20261001\",\n"
"      \"model\": {\n"
"        \"model\": \"my-device\",\n"
"        \"brand-id\": \"example-brand\",\n"
"        \"display-name\": \"My Device\"\n"
"      },\n"
"      ...\n"
"    }\n"
"  ],\n"
"  ...\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:63
msgid ""
"Select the appropriate label to [perform the pre-install checks](#perform-"
"pre-install-checks)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:65
msgid "Perform pre-install checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:67
msgid ""
"To perform the pre-install checks, use the system label to make a `GET` "
"request to `/v2/systems/{label}`. Snapd will return a synchronous response "
"(`200 OK`) with the system details. The `storage-encryption` object "
"describes the target system's storage encryption capabilities. It will state "
"whether encryption is available. If it is not available, it will list the "
"errors and the actions that can fix them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:69
msgid "Encryption is available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:71
msgid ""
"If encryption is available, `storage-encryption` will include the target "
"system's features and requirements, and no errors. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:73
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  ...\n"
"  \"storage-encryption\": {\n"
"    \"support\": \"available\",\n"
"    \"features\": [\"passphrase-auth\", \"pin-auth\"],\n"
"    \"storage-safety\": \"prefer-encrypted\",\n"
"    \"encryption-type\": \"cryptsetup\",\n"
"    \"requirements\": [\"volumes-auth\"]\n"
"  },\n"
"  ...\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:90
msgid ""
"Since there are no errors, the installation can proceed. The features and "
"requirements of the target system will be relevant when you set up the its "
"storage encryption. Skip ahead to the [Set up storage encryption section]"
"(#set-up-storage-encryption)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:92
msgid "Encryption is unavailable due to recoverable errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:94
msgid ""
"If encryption is unavailable due to recoverable errors, `storage-encryption` "
"will include `unavailable-reason` and `availability-check-errors`. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:96
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  ...\n"
"  \"storage-encryption\": {\n"
"    \"support\": \"unavailable\",\n"
"    \"features\": [\"passphrase-auth\", \"pin-auth\"],\n"
"    \"storage-safety\": \"prefer-encrypted\",\n"
"    \"unavailable-reason\": \"not encrypting device storage as checking TPM "
"gave: error with TPM2 device: TPM2 device is present but is currently "
"disabled by the platform firmware\",\n"
"    \"availability-check-errors\": [\n"
"      {\n"
"        \"kind\": \"tpm-device-disabled\",\n"
"        \"message\": \"error with TPM2 device: TPM2 device is present but is "
"currently disabled by the platform firmware\",\n"
"        \"actions\": [\n"
"          \"enable-tpm-via-firmware\",\n"
"          \"enable-and-clear-tpm-via-firmware\",\n"
"          \"reboot-to-fw-settings\"\n"
"        ]\n"
"      }\n"
"    ],\n"
"    \"requirements\": [\"volumes-auth\"]\n"
"  },\n"
"  ...\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:124
msgid ""
"In this example, the target system has a TPM 2.0 device that is disabled in "
"the firmware. This error can be resolved by executing the fix actions listed "
"in the `actions` array, in the order in which they are presented. See the "
"[Perform pre-install fix actions section](#perform-pre-install-fix-actions) "
"for guidelines and further details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:126
msgid ""
"The initial `GET` request to `/v2/systems/{label}` runs pre-install checks "
"and creates an in-memory context that will be used while fixing the errors. "
"Another `GET` request to the same endpoint replaces that context, resetting "
"the sequence of fix actions. The context is also lost if snapd restarts or "
"the system reboots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:128
msgid ""
"The table below lists error kinds that snapd might return, with a suggested "
"message to show the user, and example fix actions. The list is not "
"exhaustive: snapd can return error kinds and fix actions that the table does "
"not include. Treat it as a starting point, rather than a specification."
msgstr ""

