msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:96
msgid ""
"Either pre-OS components were authenticated with weak Authenticode digests, "
"or CAs with weak public keys were used to authenticate components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:96
msgid "`pre-os-secure-boot-auth-by-enrolled-digests`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:96
msgid ""
"Pre-OS components were authenticated by matching their Authenticode digest "
"to an entry in `db`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:96
msgid "`no-hardware-root-of-trust`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:96
msgid ""
"The platform's UEFI firmware is not verified nor measured by a hardware root "
"of trust."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:152
msgid "Encryption is unavailable due to non-recoverable errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:154
msgid ""
"If `storage-encryption` includes `unavailable-reason` but not `availability-"
"check-errors` or if `availability-check-errors` is empty, the target system "
"does not support encryption as defined in the recovery system seed. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:157
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  ...\n"
"  \"storage-encryption\": {\n"
"    \"support\": \"unavailable\",\n"
"    \"storage-safety\": \"prefer-encrypted\",\n"
"    \"unavailable-reason\": \"cannot use encryption with the gadget, "
"disabling encryption: gadget does not support encrypted data: required "
"partition with system-save role is missing\",\n"
"  },\n"
"  ...\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:172
msgid ""
"In this example, encryption is not possible because the gadget lacks a "
"system-save partition. This is a fatal error that cannot be resolved by "
"snapd. No further steps are applicable until the gadget is replaced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:174
msgid ""
"If `storage-encryption` includes `availability-check-errors`, but none of "
"the errors includes fix actions, the target system also does not support "
"encryption as defined in the recovery system seed. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:176
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  ...\n"
"  \"storage-encryption\": {\n"
"    \"support\": \"unavailable\",\n"
"    \"storage-safety\": \"prefer-encrypted\",\n"
"    \"unavailable-reason\": \"no suitable TPM2 device is available\",\n"
"    \"availability-check-errors\": [\n"
"      {\n"
"        \"kind\": \"no-suitable-tpm2-device\",\n"
"        \"message\": \"no suitable TPM2 device is available\"\n"
"      }\n"
"    ]\n"
"  }\n"
"  ...\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:197
msgid ""
"In this example, the target system's machine does not have a TPM 2.0 device "
"suitable for TPM-FDE. This is a fatal error that cannot be resolved by "
"snapd. No further steps are applicable until the hardware is replaced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:199
msgid ""
"The table below lists error kinds that snapd might return, with a suggested "
"message to show the user. The list is not exhaustive: snapd can return error "
"kinds that the table does not include. Treat it as a starting point, rather "
"than a specification."
msgstr ""

