msgid "An error occurred at the transport layer when executing a TPM command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:176
msgid "`unsupported-platform`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:176
msgid "The current host platform is not compatible with FDE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:212
msgid "Perform pre-install fix actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:215
msgid ""
"Pre-install fix actions can only be performed after an initial pre-install "
"check. See the [Perform pre-install checks section](#perform-pre-install-"
"checks) for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:218
msgid ""
"If [encryption is unavailable due to recoverable errors](#encryption-is-"
"unavailable-due-to-recoverable-errors), you can fix them by performing the "
"fix actions listed in the `actions` array of each error in `availability-"
"check-errors`. The order of the errors and their corresponding fix actions "
"should be respected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:220
msgid ""
"To perform a fix action with snapd, make a `POST` request to `/v2/systems/"
"{label}` with `action` set to `fix-encryption-support` and `fix-action` set "
"to the first entry in the error's `actions` array. For example, to enable "
"the TPM via the firmware, send this request body:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:222
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"action\": \"fix-encryption-support\",\n"
"  \"fix-action\": \"enable-tpm-via-firmware\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:229
msgid ""
"If successful, snapd will return a synchronous response (`200 OK`) with the "
"updated system details, which might include a different list of errors. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  ...\n"
"  \"storage-encryption\": {\n"
"    \"support\": \"unavailable\",\n"
"    \"features\": [\"passphrase-auth\", \"pin-auth\"],\n"
"    \"storage-safety\": \"prefer-encrypted\",\n"
"    \"unavailable-reason\": \"not encrypting device storage as checking TPM "
"gave: a reboot is required to complete the action\",\n"
"    \"availability-check-errors\": [\n"
"      {\n"
"        \"kind\": \"reboot-required\",\n"
"        \"message\": \"a reboot is required to complete the action\",\n"
"        \"actions\": [\"reboot\"]\n"
"      }\n"
"    ],\n"
"    \"requirements\": [\"volumes-auth\"]\n"
"  },\n"
"  ...\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:255
msgid ""
"In this example, the recommended fix action is to reboot the system. Since "
"this requires manual intervention from the user, this fix action cannot be "
"executed by snapd."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:257
msgid ""
"Any fix action that requires a system reboot discards the pre-install check "
"context created by the initial `GET` request to `/v2/systems/{label}`. After "
"the target system reboots, make a new `GET` request to the same endpoint to "
"create a new pre-install check context. Follow these steps again to fix any "
"lingering errors. Keep in mind that fix actions should be performed in the "
"same order in which they appear in the `actions` array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:259
msgid ""
"If snapd cannot perform an action, it will return a synchronous response "
"(`200 OK`) with the system details and updated `availability-check-errors`. "
"The table below lists error kinds that snapd might return in that situation, "
"with a suggested message to show the user, and example fix actions. The list "
"is not exhaustive: snapd can return error kinds and fix actions that the "
"table does not include. Treat it as a starting point, rather than a "
"specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "`shutdown-required`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "System shutdown is required to complete a previous action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "`shutdown`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "`reboot-required`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "System reboot is required to complete a previous action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "`reboot`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "`unexpected-action`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid ""
"The provided action is unexpected because it is either not supported or not "
"associated with the previously returned errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "none"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "`invalid-argument`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "One or more of the supplied arguments are of an invalid type or value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "`action-failed`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "The provided action did not succeed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "`missing-argument`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:231
msgid "Not enough action arguments provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:270
msgid ""
"Some of these errors, such as `unexpected-action`, `invalid-argument`, and "
"`action-failed`, offer no further fix actions. If you encounter one, make a "
"new `POST` request to `/v2/systems/{label}` with the following request body:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:272
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"action\": \"fix-encryption-support\",\n"
"  \"fix-action\": \"\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:279
msgid ""
"Setting `fix-action` to an empty string tells snapd not to perform another "
"fix action. Snapd will return a synchronous response (`200 OK`) with the "
"system details from before the previous action was attempted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:281
msgid ""
"Continue checking and resolving errors until the system details show that "
"[encryption is available](#encryption-is-available). The installation can "
"then proceed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:283
msgid "Arguments accepted by fix actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:285
msgid ""
"Most fix actions neither require nor accept arguments. There are two "
"exceptions: `proceed` and `clear-tpm`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:287
msgid ""
"The following example shows errors for which `proceed` is a possible fix "
"action:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:289
msgid "Response body, `result.storage-encryption.availability-check-errors`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:289
msgid ""
"[\n"
"  {\n"
"    \"kind\": \"addon-drivers-present\",\n"
"    \"message\": \"detected drivers running from value-added-retailer "
"components\",\n"
"    \"actions\": [\"proceed\"]\n"
"  },\n"
"  {\n"
"    \"kind\": \"weak-secure-boot-algorithms-detected\",\n"
"    \"message\": \"components were authenticated using weak Authenticode "
"digests or weak public keys\",\n"
"    \"actions\": [\"proceed\"]\n"
"  }\n"
"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:306
msgid ""
"If the fix action `proceed` is executed without arguments, snapd will ignore "
"all errors at once. This is not recommended, as it gives the user no "
"visibility into which errors are being ignored. To ignore one error at a "
"time, make a `POST` request to `/v2/systems/{label}`, passing `error-kinds` "
"in `args`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:308
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"action\": \"fix-encryption-support\",\n"
"  \"fix-action\": \"proceed\",\n"
"  \"args\": {\n"
"    \"error-kinds\": [\"<error-kind>\"]\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:319
msgid ""
"Replace `<error-kind>` with the kind of the error to ignore, as reported in "
"`availability-check-errors` (for example, `addon-drivers-present`). It is "
"recommended to list one error at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:321
msgid ""
"The fix action `clear-tpm` normally does not accept arguments. However, if "
"you attempt it against a TPM that has an auth value set in the TPM lockout "
"hierarchy, you must supply that auth value. This can happen, for example, if "
"the following error is returned:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:323
msgid ""
"Response body, one entry of `result.storage-encryption.availability-check-"
"errors`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:323
msgid ""
"\n"
"{\n"
"  \"kind\": \"tpm-hierarchies-owned\",\n"
"  \"message\": \"error with TPM2 device: one or more of the TPM hierarchies "
"is already owned\",\n"
"  \"args\": {\n"
"    \"with-auth-value\": [1073741834]\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"actions\": [\n"
"    \"clear-tpm-via-firmware\",\n"
"    \"enable-and-clear-tpm-via-firmware\",\n"
"    \"clear-tpm\",\n"
"    \"reboot-to-fw-settings\"\n"
"  ]\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:342
msgid ""
"If `clear-tpm-via-firmware` and `enable-and-clear-tpm-via-firmware` cannot "
"be performed or do not fix the issue, attempt `clear-tpm`. Make a `POST` "
"request to `/v2/systems/{label}` and pass the TPM lockout hierarchy auth "
"value, base64-encoded, in `args`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:344
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"action\": \"fix-encryption-support\",\n"
"  \"fix-action\": \"clear-tpm\",\n"
"  \"args\": {\n"
"    \"auth-value\": \"<base64-auth-value>\"\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:355
msgid ""
"Replace `<base64-auth-value>` with the base64-encoded auth value. This value "
"is chosen when the hierarchy's authorization is set and snapd cannot "
"discover it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:357
msgid ""
"In all other cases `clear-tpm` must be requested without an `args` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:359
msgid "Set up storage encryption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:361
msgid ""
"After completing the pre-install checks, you can prepare the installation of "
"Ubuntu with TPM-FDE by setting up the target system's storage encryption."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:363
msgid ""
"Depending on the target system's characteristics, adding a PIN or passphrase "
"might be supported or even required. To determine whether the target system "
"supports or requires a PIN or passphrase, look at the fields `requirements` "
"and `features` in the system details. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:365
msgid "Response body, `result.storage-encryption`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:365
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  ...\n"
"  \"features\": [\"passphrase-auth\", \"pin-auth\"],\n"
"  \"requirements\": [\"volumes-auth\"],\n"
"  ...\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:375
msgid ""
"In this example, the target system supports both PIN and passphrase as "
"authentication methods. Since `volumes-auth` is present in `requirements`, "
"at least one authentication method must be set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:377
msgid ""
"If `volumes-auth` is not present in `requirements`, setting a PIN or "
"passphrase is optional. The `features` field will tell you whether the "
"target system supports one or both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:379
msgid "Without an authentication method"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:381
msgid ""
"If the target system does not require an authentication method, you can set "
"up the storage encryption without it. Make a `POST` request to `/v2/systems/"
"{label}` with `action` set to `install`, `step` set to `setup-storage-"
"encryption`, and `on-volumes` describing the volumes to encrypt. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:383
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"action\": \"install\",\n"
"  \"step\": \"setup-storage-encryption\",\n"
"  \"on-volumes\": {\n"
"    \"pc\": {\n"
"      \"bootloader\": \"grub\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:394
msgid ""
"In this example, `on-volumes` is illustrative. Replace it with the "
"description of the volumes your installer created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:396
msgid ""
"If successful, snapd will return an asynchronous response (`202 Accepted`). "
"The response body will include a change ID. You can check the change "
"progress by making a `GET` request to `/v2/changes/{id}`. Once it completes, "
"the storage is encrypted and you can move on to the [Generate recovery key "
"section](#generate-recovery-key)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:398
msgid "With a PIN or passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:400
msgid ""
"Before setting up a PIN or passphrase, your installer should check whether "
"it meets the minimum quality requirements. This check is optional but highly "
"recommended, as it avoids errors when setting up the PIN or passphrase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:402
msgid "Check PIN or passphrase quality"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:404
msgid ""
"To check the quality of a PIN, make a `POST` request to `/v2/systems/{label}"
"` with `action` set to `check-pin-quality` and `pin` set to the PIN provided "
"by the user:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:406
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"action\": \"check-pin-quality\",\n"
"  \"pin\": \"<pin>\" \n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:413
msgid ""
"To check the quality of a passphrase, make a `POST` request to `/v2/systems/"
"{label}` with `action` set to `check-passphrase-quality` and `passphrase` "
"set to the passphrase provided by the user:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:415
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"action\": \"check-passphrase-quality\",\n"
"  \"passphrase\": \"<passphrase>\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:422
msgid ""
"If the PIN or passphrase does not meet the minimum requirements or is not "
"supported, snapd will return an error (`400 Bad Request`) and provide "
"details about the failure For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:424
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"kind\": \"invalid-pin\",\n"
"  \"message\": \"PIN did not pass quality checks\",\n"
"  \"value\": {\n"
"    \"reasons\": [\"low-entropy\"],\n"
"    \"entropy-bits\": 6,\n"
"    \"min-entropy-bits\": 13,\n"
"    \"optimal-entropy-bits\": 64\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:438
msgid "If a passphrase is tested instead, `kind` will be `invalid-passphrase`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:440
msgid ""
"If the PIN or passphrase is supported and meets the minimum requirements, "
"snapd will return a synchronous response (`200 OK`) with the entropy "
"metrics. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:442
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"entropy-bits\": 48,\n"
"  \"min-entropy-bits\": 40,\n"
"  \"optimal-entropy-bits\": 60\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:452
msgid ""
"The minimum and optimal entropy bits differ for PINs and passphrases, and "
"might change in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:454
msgid ""
"Once the PIN or passphrase meets the minimum requirements, it can be added "
"to the storage encryption setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:456
msgid "Add PIN or passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:458
msgid ""
"To add a PIN, make a `POST` request to `/v2/systems/{label}` with `action` "
"set to `install` and `step` set to `setup-storage-encryption`. The request "
"body must also include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:459
msgid "`on-volumes`, describing the volumes to encrypt;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:460
msgid "`volumes-auth` with the PIN; and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:461
msgid ""
"`keyboard-config`, describing the keyboard configuration selected by the "
"user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:463
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:465
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"action\": \"install\",\n"
"  \"step\": \"setup-storage-encryption\",\n"
"  \"on-volumes\": {\n"
"    \"pc\": {\n"
"      \"bootloader\": \"grub\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"volumes-auth\": {\n"
"    \"mode\": \"pin\",\n"
"    \"pin\": \"<pin>\"\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"keyboard-config\": {\n"
"    \"model\": \"pc105\",\n"
"    \"layout\": \"us\"\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:484
msgid ""
"In this example, `on-volumes` is illustrative. Replace it with the "
"description of the volumes your installer created. `keyboard-config` is also "
"illustrative. Set it to the keyboard layout the user selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:486
msgid ""
"To add a passphrase instead, replace `volumes-auth` in the request body "
"above with one including the user's passphrase:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:487
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"volumes-auth\": {\n"
"    \"mode\": \"passphrase\",\n"
"    \"passphrase\": \"<passphrase>\"\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:496
msgid ""
"When adding a PIN or passphrase to the storage encryption setup, `keyboard-"
"config` must be defined. Snapd uses this configuration to ensure that the "
"same keyboard layout is available when the user enters the PIN or passphrase "
"on first boot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:498
msgid ""
"If successful, snapd will return an asynchronous response (`202 Accepted`). "
"The response body will include a change ID. You can check its progress by "
"making a `GET` request to `/v2/changes/{id}`. Once it completes, the storage "
"is encrypted and you can move to the next step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:500
msgid "Generate recovery key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:502
msgid ""
"Generating a recovery key is optional, but highly recommended. A recovery "
"key is a high-entropy fallback credential used to recover the data on the "
"disk if all other methods fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:504
msgid ""
"To generate a recovery key, make a `POST` request to `/v2/systems/{label}`, "
"with the following request body:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:506
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"action\": \"install\",\n"
"  \"step\": \"generate-recovery-key\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:513
msgid ""
"Snapd will return a synchronous response (`200 OK`) with the recovery key. "
"For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:515
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"recovery-key\": \"12345-67890-12345-67890-12345-67890-12345-67890\"\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:523
msgid ""
"Present the recovery key to the user and tell them clearly that, in the "
"event of hardware failure, they might lose their data without it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:526
msgid "Make the target system bootable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:528
msgid ""
"To make the target system bootable, send a `POST` request to `/v2/systems/"
"{label}` with `action` set to `install`, `step` set to `finish`, and `on-"
"volumes` describing those volumes. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:530
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"action\": \"install\",\n"
"  \"step\": \"finish\",\n"
"  \"on-volumes\": {\n"
"    \"pc\": {\n"
"      \"bootloader\": \"grub\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:541
msgid ""
"In this example, `on-volumes` is illustrative. Reuse the `on-volumes` value "
"from the storage encryption setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:543
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:580
msgid ""
"If successful, snapd will return an asynchronous response (`202 Accepted`). "
"The response body will include a change ID. Wait until the change is "
"complete before moving to the next step. You can check its progress by "
"making a `GET` request to `/v2/changes/{id}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:545
msgid ""
"Once the change is complete, snapd has written the following onto the target "
"system's volumes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:546
msgid "the gadget content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:547
msgid "the kernel snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:548
msgid "the base snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:549
msgid "the gadget snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:550
msgid "the bootloader configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:551
msgid "the `modeenv`, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:552
msgid "the disk-unlock keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:554
msgid ""
"The system is now ready to reboot and install Ubuntu with TPM-FDE, but it is "
"highly recommended to preseed it first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:556
msgid "Preseed the target system before first boot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:558
msgid ""
"Preseeding the target system before the first boot is optional, but highly "
"recommended. It makes the first boot faster and detects potential failures "
"early."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:560
msgid ""
"Before preseeding, create the following mount points to match the existing "
"preseeding workflow:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:561
msgid "`/dev`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:562
msgid "`/proc`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:563
msgid "`/sys`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:564
msgid "`/sys/kernel/security`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:566
msgid ""
"Snapd's preseeding checks require `/sys` and `/sys/kernel/security` to be "
"mounted independently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:568
msgid ""
"Also, bind-mount the installer environment's seed directory into `<target-"
"root>/var/lib/snapd/seed`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:570
msgid ""
"To preseed the target system, make a `POST` request to `/v2/systems/{label}` "
"with `action` set to `install`, `step` set to `preseed`, and `target-root` "
"set to the mount point of the installer target system's decrypted system-"
"data filesystem:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:572
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"action\": \"install\",\n"
"  \"step\": \"preseed\",\n"
"  \"target-root\": \"<target-root>\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/install-with-tpm-fde.md:582
msgid ""
"When preseeding is complete, the target system is ready to reboot and "
"install Ubuntu with TPM-FDE."
msgstr ""
